---

# mcu-shell-sd

apps/mcu-shell with the board's SD card as well: the board's own storage at
/data through mm.fs.local, and the FAT volume on the card in the board's
socket at /sd through mm.sdcard.socket and mm.fs.fat. It is a separate
application because selecting it is the build option that brings FatFs and
the card driver into the image; mcu-shell stays without them. It builds only
on a board that binds mm.sdcard.socket. An empty socket, or a card holding no
FAT volume, still gets the shell, with a line saying so; the card is never
formatted. sd mounts the card again after one is inserted.
